# BUILD FLOW 01.03 — .gitattributes
# First introduced: Phase 01
# Purpose: Make line endings predictable. We edit on Windows (CRLF line endings) but run
#          scripts in Linux containers, CI, and on EC2 (LF). A shell script with CRLF
#          endings fails on Linux with errors such as "$'\r': command not found".
# Depends on: Git reading this file on every checkout and commit.
# Used by: Git. These rules override this machine's system-wide core.autocrlf=true setting.
# Runtime role: None at application runtime; it shapes every file later phases commit.
#
# Syntax: "<pattern> <attribute>[=value] ...". Later lines win when patterns overlap.

# BUILD FLOW 01.03.01 — Default rule: text files use LF, in the repository and on disk
# text=auto lets Git detect whether a file is text. eol=lf checks text files out with LF
# too, so files copied into Linux images are already correct.
* text=auto eol=lf

# BUILD FLOW 01.03.02 — Windows-only scripts keep CRLF
# cmd.exe can misread batch files saved with LF endings. PowerShell scripts follow the same
# Windows convention. (The Maven Wrapper's mvnw.cmd from Phase 02 matches *.cmd.)
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# BUILD FLOW 01.03.03 — Binary files: never convert line endings, never diff as text
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
